  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A plane electromagnetic wave propagating in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-direction is described by<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo></math>The intensity of the wave is :<br/>(Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>",
