  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The magnitude of the electric field component of the electromagnetic wave is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the intensity of the electromagnetic wave is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn></msub><mi>c</mi><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msubsup><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>53</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
